        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.065,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Lines and Angles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.12,
            0.554,
            0.141
          ],
          "content": "Did you include angles such as ∠TOQ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.143,
            0.704,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "Which set of markings did you use — inner or outer?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.166,
            0.472,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "What is the measure of ∠TOS?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.191,
            0.833,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "Can you use the numbers marked to find the angle without counting the number of markings?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.236,
            0.834,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "Here, OT and OS pass through the numbers 20 and 55 on the outer scale. How many units of 1 degree are contained between these two arms?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.303,
            0.47,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "Can subtraction be used here?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.335,
            0.833,
            0.356
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "How can we measure angles directly without having to subtract?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.364,
            0.777,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "Place the protractor so the center is on the vertex of the angle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.387,
            0.834,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "Align the protractor so that one the arms passes through the 0º mark as in the picture below."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.43,
            0.744,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
