        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.66,
            0.521,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": "What is the degree measure of $\\angle  AOB?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.688,
            0.426,
            0.708
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Make your own Protractor!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.716,
            0.833,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "You may have wondered how the different equally spaced markings are made on a protractor. We will now see how we can make some of them!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.761,
            0.833,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "1. Draw a circle of a convenient radius on a sheet of paper. Cut out the circle (Fig. 2.13). A circle or one full turn is 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.806,
            0.835,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": "2. Fold the circle to get two equal halves and cut it through the crease to get a semicircle. Write ‘0°’ in the bottom right corner of the semicircle."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.888,
            0.942,
            0.912,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": "37"
        }
      ]
    }
